  "scope": "Complete compact projective strict-Lelong-level counterexample, with a natural-home proof, history/index seams and checked publication.",
  "mathematical_boundary": "Positive closed (1,1)-current and quasi-psh example on P2; the non-strict threshold remains analytic. No new original closure, full current-transform proof or broad pluriharmonic Siu adoption.",
  "mathematics": {
    "method": "Direct compact projective example reconstructed from explicit potentials and dominated radial trace limits; no solver verdict",
    "count": 23,
    "obligations": [
      {
        "name": "Homogeneity",
        "check": "Both logarithmic quotients are invariant under common nonzero homogeneous scaling.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Unit normalization",
        "check": "The coefficient vector of x-a_j z has squared norm 1+a_j squared; its quotient is nonpositive by Cauchy--Schwarz.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Curvature normalization",
        "check": "With the book ddc, Poincare--Lelong gives ddc log of a unit linear quotient equals the line current minus normalized sigma.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Summability",
        "check": "lambda_j=2^(-j-1) sums to 1/2.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Unitary action",
        "check": "U(3) acts on coordinates, preserves Fubini--Study measure and is transitive on unit linear forms.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Uniform integrability",
        "check": "A logarithmic hyperplane pole is locally integrable; invariance gives one finite global L1 norm for every unit linear form.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Monotone finite limit",
        "check": "Nonpositive summands and summable uniform L1 norms give an L1 decreasing limit, excluding an identically minus infinity limit.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Uniform curvature",
        "check": "Finite sums have lower bound -(1+sum_{j<=N}lambda_j)sigma >= -3sigma/2.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Genuine quasi-psh representative",
        "check": "Local smooth corrections make all partial sums psh; their nontrivial decreasing limit is the quasi-psh representative.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Current series",
        "check": "Line trace mass is degree one; summable positive measures give a finite positive closed current series.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Derivative and limit",
        "check": "Distributional ddc commutes with the established L1 limit, giving T=[D]+sum lambda_j[L_j].",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Local radial normalization",
        "check": "In affine complex dimension two, book kappa restricts to normalized Euclidean area on each affine complex line.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Exact line-ball mass",
        "check": "An affine line at distance d intersects a Euclidean radius-r ball in a complex disc of squared radius (r squared-d squared)_+.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Uniform normalized bound",
        "check": "Each line contributes between zero and one after division by r squared, uniformly over all indices and radii.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Trace interchange",
        "check": "Positivity permits Tonelli for the line-current trace on every ball.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Limit interchange",
        "check": "The summable coefficient majorant permits dominated convergence as r decreases to zero, including accumulating lines.",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Function-current Lelong identity",
        "check": "A smooth local potential of the background changes no Lelong number; the classical mass formula identifies nu(u,q) with nu(T,q).",
        "status": "scoped checked"
      },
      {
        "name": "Intersection geometry",
        "check": "Distinct x-a_j z lines meet only at [0:1:0], while D meets them at [a_j:0:1].",
